{
  "slug": "using-cmux",
  "name": "Using Cmux",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "A Claude Code plugin that teaches the agent to operate cmux, a terminal multiplexer with first-class agent integration. Provides skill patterns and shell wrappers (cmux-send, cmux-read, cmux-send-key, cmux-grid, cfork) for the full sub-agent lifecycle: launch -> trust detection -> prompt -> completion detection -> result collection. Browser automation is covered to the depth needed for a single agent. Companion plugin cmux-team handles multi-agent orchestration on top of using-cmux. macOS / Linux only.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill** and **2 commands**.\n\n- **Skills** (1): `using-cmux` (cmux ターミナル内での操作スキル。ペイン分割、サブエージェント起動・監視・結果回収、コマンド送信、画面読み取り、通知に使用。CMUX_* 環境変数が存在する場合にトリガーされる。)\n- **Commands** (2): `cfork`, `cmux`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install using-cmux@claude-community` from `hummer98/using-cmux`.\n\n日本語 | English\n\nA Claude Code plugin that teaches the agent to operate cmux, a terminal multiplexer with first-class agent integration. Provides skill patterns and shell wrappers (cmux-send, cmux-read, cmux-send-key, cmux-grid, cfork) for the full sub-agent lifecycle: launch -> trust detection -> prompt -> completion detection -> result collection. Browser automation is covered to the depth needed for a single agent. Companion plugin cmux-team handles multi-agent orchestration on top of using-cmux. macOS / Linux only.",
